{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Test Estimation Good Practices"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about software testing elements."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Implement and document the software tests, applying trial and error, based on the designed plan and procedures established by the company.  Applies the different types of software testing to the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on software testing, test estimation, and data migration processes Narrative Scenario"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "time frame"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The core of estimating time is the time frame per se."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stick to"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to follow something strictly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's utterly important to stick to the due dates for every stage without putting aside the unpredictable factors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "buffer time"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extra time assigned to a project to avoid readjustment of the original schedule"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Allow buffer time, and try to take into account unexpected events that may occur and delay the development of the project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "budget"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "money available to be used for a specific purpose"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The last element is cost where you will have to plan the budget for the project."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "foresee"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to predict something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now, some recommendations for time estimation is to foresee the bug cycle."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p><strong>Phrasal verbs</strong> are expressions formed with a verb and a preposition to create new and different meanings.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Before starting software testing, break down the project so it will be easier to assign roles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p><strong>Phrasal verbs</strong> are commonly used in English. Whether it is in formal or informal conversations, they make up an important part of the language usage.</p> <p>Most common <strong>phrasal verbs</strong> are <strong>verbs</strong> with <strong>one preposition,</strong> but there are some others with <strong>two </strong>or<strong> three prepositions</strong>. They can also be separable or inseparable, meaning that the object of the sentence can go in between the verb and the preposition.</p> <p>Verbs working with different prepositions may have a different meaning from the sole verb and sometimes they tend to be easily confused. However, it&rsquo;s a matter of practicing.</p> <p>Some <strong>phrasal verbs</strong> are:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pick out</strong>: To <strong>pick</strong> something <strong>out </strong>= to choose</li> <li><strong>Look for</strong>: To <strong>look for</strong> = to search something</li> <li><strong>Break down</strong>: To <strong>break</strong> something <strong>down</strong> = to divide into small parts</li> </ul> <p>Examples:</p> <p><i>We need to <strong>look for</strong> the best workers for our project to be finished on time.</i></p> <p><i>We will save time if we <strong>break down</strong> each part of the project.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's essential to carefully pick out human resources and equipment as they will be the pillars of the project. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Be sure to look for the best and most qualified people since they will help you to achieve your goals and therefore saving you time and money."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Elements to be Estimated in Software Testing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are crucial factors that require extra planning in software testing that if planned well, they will make life easier. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Such factors need to work fluently with each other as they are linked in a way that involves all stages and parts of the software to be tested.</p> <p>There are different ways of calculating <i>how much</i> or <i>how many.</i> You will need to complete the project but time is something you can&rsquo;t spare or squander. Try to cover all the situations that may happen as your team goes through the project, so in the case of any of those extraordinary situations happen, you won&rsquo;t have to readjust the schedule which will be traumatic to the development of other activities.</p> <p>Those factors include physical resources such as computers; human resources such as programmers or testers; and facilities such as buildings, offices, and equipment. The second element is time. You will have to carefully plan the schedule. The third element is human skills in which hiring people who have the right qualities for the project becomes crucial. And the last element is the cost, which includes payment, purchasing, rent, etc.&nbsp;</p>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Draw a poster with each testing software element."}, {"type": "text", "content": " In each poster write a brave description of their characteristics."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use phrasal verbs and relative clauses. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the four posters with your class and explain them."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I know the four testing software elements."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I write the characteristics of each element."}, {"type": "text", "content": " I talk about the four testing elements"}, {"type": "text", "content": " I use phrasal verbs and relative clauses in a correct way."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the elements that should be included when testing a software."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe good test estimation practices."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What would you do if you run out of time to hand in an important project?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Is it important to have a B plan whe